---
// Optimized assets are now referenced via public paths in /assets/optimized/
import Landing from '../components/Landing.astro';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import '../styles/studio.css';

const belongs = ['Manuscript', 'Lore', 'Timeline', 'Plot Maps', 'Knowledge Graph'];
---

<Base
  title="Studio"
  description="Miraforge Studio is a desktop workspace for writers and other creative professionals. The manuscript, lore, timelines, structure, and supporting material live together in one Archive."
>
  <Landing
    hero
    eyebrow="Miraforge Studio"
    title="A creative workspace built around the work itself"
    lead="Write, organize, explore, and develop complex creative projects without scattering them across disconnected tools."
    seal="/assets/optimized/wax_book__orig.webp"
    plate="/assets/optimized/CandlelightStudioDesktop__1920w.webp"
    plateAlt="An open manuscript on a worktable, surrounded by maps, index cards, drafting tools, and bound volumes."
  >
    <p>
      Miraforge Studio is a desktop workspace for writers and other creative professionals. It
      brings the manuscript, lore, timelines, structure, relationships, and supporting material
      together inside a single project Archive.
    </p>
    <p>The goal is simple: keep the tools close to the work, without letting the tools become the work.</p>
    <Fragment slot="after">
      <div class="studio-story">
        <section class="studio-block">
          <div class="studio-copy">
            <h2>Everything belongs to the work</h2>
            <p>Creative projects rarely live in a manuscript alone.</p>
            <p>
              Characters accumulate histories. Places gain detail. Timelines become complicated.
              Ideas move. Scenes change purpose. Research piles up. Connections emerge that were
              never planned at the beginning.
            </p>
            <p>Studio is designed around that reality.</p>
            <p>
              Instead of treating those materials as separate files or separate applications, Studio
              keeps them together inside an Archive: a durable home for the work and the knowledge
              surrounding it.
            </p>
          </div>
          <figure class="studio-figure">
            <picture>
                          <source type="image/avif" srcset="/assets/optimized/stilllife_everything__640w.avif 640w, /assets/optimized/stilllife_everything__1024w.avif 1024w, /assets/optimized/stilllife_everything__1920w.avif 1920w" sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, (max-width: 1024px) 50vw, 800px">
                          <source type="image/webp" srcset="/assets/optimized/stilllife_everything__640w.webp 640w, /assets/optimized/stilllife_everything__1024w.webp 1024w, /assets/optimized/stilllife_everything__1920w.webp 1920w" sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, (max-width: 1024px) 50vw, 800px">
                          <img
                            src="/assets/optimized/stilllife_everything__1024w.webp"
                            width="1024"
                            height="768"
                            alt="An open folio surrounded by character studies, a map, a timeline, and a web of relationships."
                            loading="lazy"
                          />
                        </picture>
            <ul class="studio-cluster">
              {belongs.map((name) => <li>{name}</li>)}
            </ul>
          </figure>
        </section>

        <section class="studio-block is-flip">
          <figure class="studio-figure">
            <picture>
                          <source type="image/avif" srcset="/assets/optimized/stillife_notes__640w.avif 640w, /assets/optimized/stillife_notes__1024w.avif 1024w, /assets/optimized/stillife_notes__1920w.avif 1920w" sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, (max-width: 1024px) 50vw, 800px">
                          <source type="image/webp" srcset="/assets/optimized/stillife_notes__640w.webp 640w, /assets/optimized/stillife_notes__1024w.webp 1024w, /assets/optimized/stillife_notes__1920w.webp 1920w" sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, (max-width: 1024px) 50vw, 800px">
                          <img
                            src="/assets/optimized/stillife_notes__1024w.webp"
                            width="1024"
                            height="768"
                            alt="A desk covered in handwritten notes, index cards, and sketches." loading="lazy"
                            loading="lazy"
                          />
                        </picture>
          </figure>
          <div class="studio-copy">
            <h2>Structure without forcing a method</h2>
            <p>Writers work differently.</p>
            <p>
              Some plan extensively before writing. Others discover the story as they go. Some think
              in scenes, some in timelines, some in relationships, and some simply need a place to
              keep the growing mass of a project understandable.
            </p>
            <p>Studio provides structure without prescribing a creative method.</p>
            <p>
              Use as much or as little of it as the work requires. The tools are there to support
              the process, not dictate it.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="studio-block">
          <div class="studio-copy">
            <h2>Built for projects that grow</h2>
            <p>A novel can begin as a few pages and end with years of accumulated material.</p>
            <p>Studio is being built for that entire journey.</p>
            <p>
              Its deeper tools help you follow relationships, understand chronology, navigate large
              bodies of lore, and maintain context as the project becomes more complex.
            </p>
            <p>
              The same Archive that holds an early draft can grow with the work rather than being
              replaced by a collection of increasingly fragile files and applications.
            </p>
            <p class="studio-callout">One Archive. One body of work. Many ways to understand it.</p>
          </div>
          <figure class="studio-figure">
            <picture>
                          <source type="image/avif" srcset="/assets/optimized/stilllife_research__640w.avif 640w, /assets/optimized/stilllife_research__1024w.avif 1024w, /assets/optimized/stilllife_research__1920w.avif 1920w" sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, (max-width: 1024px) 50vw, 800px">
                          <source type="image/webp" srcset="/assets/optimized/stilllife_research__640w.webp 640w, /assets/optimized/stilllife_research__1024w.webp 1024w, /assets/optimized/stilllife_research__1920w.webp 1920w" sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, (max-width: 1024px) 50vw, 800px">
                          <img
                            src="/assets/optimized/stilllife_research__1024w.webp"
                            width="1024"
                            height="768"
                            alt="An open research volume with a card file, maps, and connected reference cards."
                            loading="lazy"
                          />
                        </picture>
          </figure>
        </section>

        <section class="studio-block is-flip">
          <figure class="studio-figure">
            <picture>
                          <source type="image/avif" srcset="/assets/optimized/stilllife_ai_section__640w.avif 640w, /assets/optimized/stilllife_ai_section__1024w.avif 1024w, /assets/optimized/stilllife_ai_section__1920w.avif 1920w" sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, (max-width: 1024px) 50vw, 800px">
                          <source type="image/webp" srcset="/assets/optimized/stilllife_ai_section__640w.webp 640w, /assets/optimized/stilllife_ai_section__1024w.webp 1024w, /assets/optimized/stilllife_ai_section__1920w.webp 1920w" sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, (max-width: 1024px) 50vw, 800px">
                          <img
                            src="/assets/optimized/stilllife_ai_section__1024w.webp"
                            width="1024"
                            height="768"
                            alt="An open ledger of connected sketches, with a card file and drafting tools beside it."
                            loading="lazy"
                          />
                        </picture>
          </figure>
          <div class="studio-copy">
            <h2>AI is optional. Useful is mandatory.</h2>
            <p>Studio is not built around generative AI, and AI is never required to use it.</p>
            <p>Where AI is used, our standard is simple: it should solve a real problem.</p>
            <p>
              That may mean helping locate information across a large Archive, checking continuity,
              organizing material, or handling work that would otherwise interrupt the creative
              process.
            </p>
            <p>
              We are less interested in AI that generates for you than in AI that helps Studio
              understand the work you have already created.
            </p>
            <p class="studio-credo">The writer remains the author. The software remains the tool.</p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="studio-block">
          <div class="studio-copy">
            <h2>Built to become more than a novel-writing tool</h2>
            <p>Studio begins with long-form fiction because that is the problem we know best.</p>
            <p>
              But stories and creative projects take many forms. Screenplays, stage works, serial
              fiction, tabletop campaigns, nonfiction, and other forms of structured creative work
              share many of the same underlying needs: content, knowledge, relationships,
              chronology, and organization.
            </p>
            <p>Studio is being designed with that broader future in mind.</p>
          </div>
          <figure class="studio-figure">
            <picture>
                          <source type="image/avif" srcset="/assets/optimized/stilllife_planning__640w.avif 640w, /assets/optimized/stilllife_planning__1024w.avif 1024w, /assets/optimized/stilllife_planning__1920w.avif 1920w" sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, (max-width: 1024px) 50vw, 800px">
                          <source type="image/webp" srcset="/assets/optimized/stilllife_planning__640w.webp 640w, /assets/optimized/stilllife_planning__1024w.webp 1024w, /assets/optimized/stilllife_planning__1920w.webp 1920w" sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, (max-width: 1024px) 50vw, 800px">
                          <img
                            src="/assets/optimized/stilllife_planning__1024w.webp"
                            width="1024"
                            height="768"
                            alt="An open planning book with scene sketches, loose outlines, and stacks of reference volumes."
                            loading="lazy"
                          />
                        </picture>
          </figure>
        </section>

        <section class="studio-block is-flip studio-close">
          <figure class="studio-figure">
            <picture>
                          <source type="image/avif" srcset="/assets/optimized/stilllife_keep_creating__640w.avif 640w, /assets/optimized/stilllife_keep_creating__1024w.avif 1024w, /assets/optimized/stilllife_keep_creating__1920w.avif 1920w" sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, (max-width: 1024px) 50vw, 800px">
                          <source type="image/webp" srcset="/assets/optimized/stilllife_keep_creating__640w.webp 640w, /assets/optimized/stilllife_keep_creating__1024w.webp 1024w, /assets/optimized/stilllife_keep_creating__1920w.webp 1920w" sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, (max-width: 1024px) 50vw, 800px">
                          <img
                            src="/assets/optimized/stilllife_keep_creating__1024w.webp"
                            width="1024"
                            height="768"
                            alt="A closed journal with a compass rose, resting on maps, sketches, and bound volumes."
                            loading="lazy"
                          />
                        </picture>
          </figure>
          <div class="studio-copy">
            <h2>Keep the work together. Keep creating.</h2>
            <p>Miraforge Studio exists to reduce the distance between an idea and the work of developing it.</p>
            <p>
              Fewer disconnected tools. Less time hunting for context. More confidence that the
              project remains understandable as it grows.
            </p>
            <p>
              The software should help you hold the shape of the work in your mind — and then get out
              of the way.
            </p>
            <div class="landing-actions">
              <a class="btn btn-primary btn-brass" href="/studio/">Explore Studio</a>
              <button class="btn btn-brass-inverse" type="button" disabled>See Features</button>
              <button class="btn btn-brass-inverse" type="button" disabled>Join the Beta</button>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </div>
    </Fragment>
  </Landing>
</Base>
